# Get a free access key at https://web3forms.com (enter the inbox email you
# want submissions delivered to, e.g. talharehman01997@gmail.com — the key
# arrives by email instantly, no account or password needed).
#
# Must use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix: the contact form submits directly from
# the visitor's browser to Web3Forms (not through our own server), because
# Web3Forms' upstream bot protection blocks requests coming from cloud/
# server IP ranges (Vercel, AWS, etc.) even with valid keys. This is
# Web3Forms' documented, intended usage pattern — the key is safe to expose
# client-side by design.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are baked in at BUILD time, so after adding/changing
# this you must trigger a new deployment (not just a redeploy of the same
# build) for it to take effect.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
